1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,244
A Signal Group turns several signals into one reading:

2
00:00:03,294 --> 00:00:08,095
a score from minus one hundred to plus one hundred, and a label, such as Bullish.

3
00:00:08,532 --> 00:00:10,308
You can start from a starter Group,

4
00:00:10,328 --> 00:00:14,528
the same ones behind the dashboard's pre-configured Trend, Stretch and Flow,

5
00:00:14,578 --> 00:00:16,905
or from scratch. Let's build our own.

6
00:00:17,346 --> 00:00:20,334
Add signals by dragging them in, or tapping plus.

7
00:00:20,384 --> 00:00:24,161
Here: moving averages, the Ichimoku cloud, and the MACD line.

8
00:00:24,597 --> 00:00:28,844
Each signal has a role. Score signals are combined into the Group's score.

9
00:00:28,894 --> 00:00:33,610
Condition signals are only used in rules, and Context is shown alongside.

10
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:38,297
Rules give the labels, checked from the top: the first that matches wins.

11
00:00:38,347 --> 00:00:42,123
At least plus thirty is Bullish. At most minus thirty is Bearish.

12
00:00:42,143 --> 00:00:43,553
Otherwise, Neutral.

13
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:48,385
If a rule can't be checked because a reading is missing, the label is Unknown,

14
00:00:48,435 --> 00:00:49,844
never a guess.

15
00:00:50,314 --> 00:00:53,046
Vetoes protect you from the wrong conditions.

16
00:00:53,096 --> 00:00:57,279
Here, if the daily market is ranging, every label becomes Vetoed.

17
00:01:02,394 --> 00:01:06,086
The checks tell you what blocks saving, and what is only a warning.

18
00:01:06,136 --> 00:01:09,103
And the description is written for you, in plain words.

19
00:01:09,544 --> 00:01:13,599
Name it, and save. It's yours, and private, until you publish it.

20
00:01:13,649 --> 00:01:17,938
Changing it later saves a new version, so earlier ones stay as they were.

21
00:01:23,315 --> 00:01:25,663
Why it helps: your reading of the trend,

22
00:01:25,713 --> 00:01:28,168
the same every time, on every asset.
